{:title
 "Composing from Inside a Prompt, Editing a Rendered Smile Prompt Back Into Its Pieces",
 :description
 "What composing from inside a prompt is in THE MAP of Smile, a render that is writable, where every changed word reaches the piece that wrote it and the magnification of an edit sets the tier that keeps it, and how my words reached it on 10 and 11 August 2026, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "editable prompt render, composing from inside a prompt, prompt overrides, edit the compiled prompt, modular prompt editing, Smile prompt language, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, a render is writable and a prompt is somewhere to write. Words changed in a finished prompt are written into the piece that wrote them, and the composition comes back changed.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP lists what each act does from inside a render. Words changed are written into the piece that wrote them. A part deleted is removed from the gathering while its words remain in the Field. Parts reordered reorder the gathering. A module's words pasted make the composition gather that module, live. New writing is registered to the composition as a new raw text. A delimiter changed reaches the face at that position. All of this rests on the way back, every line of a render knowing which piece wrote it and how far it was indented."
 "In THE MAP, the magnification an edit is made at is the tier that keeps it. At the tier of the pieces the piece itself changes and everything gathering it comes back changed. At a tier above, the change is kept there as an override and the pieces below remain as they are. Several tiers can be selected before typing, and the selection is the reach, so changing a mark everywhere and changing one line are the same edit at two magnifications. Each act is to be proven, composed again to show what was saved, or every file restored exactly."
 "I asked for it on two days of August 2026 on my PC. On 10 August I asked for “a navigation system where e..g. you can view a composition as the text it is, edit that text, and it actually edits the modules it is connected to, but from your viewer you are just editing a prompt.”, then “you can edit any renders at any time to make the changes you are interested in. implement this so that I can work”, and “you can edit that main text file in the section you want to make changes, and it applies across all of it.”[[m:2026-08-10]]"
 "On 11 August I set where an edit lands. “if you want to adjust an instructions text, then you would, in the composition level, make that edit, and then that edit is saved to t he compositon, so that lets you edit nested compositions at the level you are viewing them.”, and “So we have an overwrite at the composition level. We have overwrites at any level.”[[m:2026-08-11]] That is the tier rule THE MAP keeps, an edit kept at the magnification it was made at, which is still to be built."
 "Across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes, from {{first}} to {{last}}, I asked in two days for the render to be made into a place to write. Carrying hand edits back into the modules is part built, and editing at a chosen magnification is still to be built. The tiers an edit is made at are followed in [[t:magnification]], the overrides in [[t:composition]], and the editor around it in [[t:the-editor]]."],
